WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.868
-Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs,

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.601
and we especially love songs
written by our audience members

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.100
in under an hour.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.467
It's time for "Battle of
the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.868
Here we go.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.834
-♪ Something song,
and I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:19.133
♪ And I'm writing a song
about another song ♪

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.567
-Welcome to "Battle of
the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.467
Now, before the show,
we went through our audience

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.133
and picked out people --
two people --

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.934
who said that
they were musicians.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.501
We gave them each
a made-up song title --

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.868
You don't have to be,
but you said that you were,

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.901
so we'll see if they were.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.133
Now, we gave them
an hour to write

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.534
an original song
based on that title.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.267
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.868
Oh, two guitarists.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.501
They're going for it.
All right, here we go.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:46.734
I can't wait to see
what they came up with.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.901
Let's meet them right now.
Come on over, guys!

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.667
Our contestants, welcome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.334
Hello.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.834
Nice to see you.
Welcome. Thank you.

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:58.501
Nice to see you.
Welcome.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.367
Yeah!
Welcome to the show!

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.400
Thank you for being here.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.767
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.467
-Let's start with
contestant number one.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:06.934
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.901
-My name is Victoria Skie,
and I am from New Jersey.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.100
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.601
Victoria Skie -- great name.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.501
What was the --
what was the title of the song

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.701
that you were given?

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.567
-The title was
"I Still Don't Understand NFTs."

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.234
-Ah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.901
That's very -- That's very good.
I like that.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.834
I can't wait
to hear this song, yeah.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.634
I'm just figuring it out myself.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:29.767
What instrument
will you be playing?

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:30.834
The guitar?
-Guitar.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.300
-Yeah, perfect.
All right, go get ready.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.133
And whenever you're set...
Get comfortable.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Now this is a big deal.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.801
You can scoot over here,
if you'd like.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.200
Yeah.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.767
Ladies and gentlemen, here to
perform the world premiere

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:46.701
of the soon-to-be classic,
"I Still Don't Understand NFTs,"

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.634
it's Victoria Skie!

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:51.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:54.968
♪♪

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:57.834
-♪ Since I was a little girl ♪

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:01.400
♪ I've loved to doodle hearts
and swirls ♪

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:07.534
♪ And draw my family
like ugly sticks ♪

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:11.000
♪ Yeah, they were never
any good ♪

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.334
♪ Oh, but now we live
in a different world ♪

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:18.934
♪ And my uncle old me he thinks
I could get rich ♪

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.834
♪ Real quick ♪

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:24.000
♪ It's something 'bout crypto ♪

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.033
♪ Went over my head ♪

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:33.434
♪ Guess these monkeys
ain't jumping on any more beds ♪

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.634
♪ Now they're worth
a million dollars ♪

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.767
♪ Oh, I wish that could be me ♪

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:44.434
♪ But I still
don't understand NFTs ♪

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.567
♪ Why can't we
just screenshot them? ♪

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.701
♪♪

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:59.701
♪ What currency
even buys them? ♪

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:03.300
♪ I guess
they're just untouchable ♪

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.200
♪ And something
'bout non-fungible ♪

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.167
♪ But I still
don't understand NFTs ♪

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:17.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.734
-Man, that's not bad.
That's -- yeah.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.834
Victoria Skie, everybody!

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:26.334
That was incredible.
That was phenomenal.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:29.400
Thank you so much.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.000
-Good luck, buddy.
Uh...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.100
Contestant number two,
what is your name,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.267
and where are you from, pal?

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.234
-My name is Asa Daniels,
and I'm from Long Island.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, good man.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.567
We love Long Island.
Thanks, Asa Daniels.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:44.701
Great names.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:47.234
What -- What title
were you given today?

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.434
-Sure. They gave me
"Batman Spoilers."

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:50.801
[ Laughter ]
-Ooh.

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.767
Be very careful with this song,
yeah, 'cause we don't

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.801
want to hear any "Batman"
spoilers, but -- you might.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.267
You might.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.033
Wow. Have you seen the new
"Batman" movie?

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:00.767
-I have not.
-There you go.

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.334
-I'm guessing.
-Perfect.

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.234
Yeah, this is a perfect song
for you, "Batman Spoilers."

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:06.501
And you're playing the guitar,
as well?

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:07.701
-Yeah, that's right.
In my band,

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.133
I play guitar, and I sing.
-I love that, bud.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.267
-Later tonight.
-Let's do it.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:11.834
Let's go for it.
Yeah, go get ready.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.767
A very talented audience.
Come on over here, pal.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:20.734
♪♪

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:21.901
And I just want
to remind everyone,

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.000
he has not seen
the new "Batman" movie.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.100
Ladies and gentlemen,
get ready for the world premiere

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.567
of "Batman Spoilers,"
by Asa Daniels!

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:34.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.968
-♪ It's Wednesday night ♪

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:39.100
♪ I'm just hanging
with my friends ♪

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:45.801
♪ Someone says,
"Let's go and see 'Batman'" ♪

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.667
♪ Maybe they'll have cameos ♪

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:51.000
♪ From all the
past movies like ♪

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.534
♪ Bale and Keaton
and my boy George Clooney ♪

00:04:56.534 --> 00:05:02.234
♪ I've got some spoilers
of my own to tell ♪

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.133
♪ Joker joined the Girl Scouts ♪

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:07.968
♪ And he's got
some cookies to sell ♪

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:13.067
♪ Alfred plays kickball
with Commissioner Gordon ♪

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:17.267
♪ And I heard
it's now a musical ♪

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:19.467
♪ And it's starring
James Corden ♪

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:22.367
♪ Catwoman blows
all of her money ♪

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:25.300
♪ Buying cans of Fancy Feast ♪

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.067
♪ Riddler's riddles
are just Wordle ♪

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.734
♪ And he breaks up
Batman's streak ♪

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:33.167
♪ Bruce Wayne
is rich and famous ♪

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.534
♪ He's got a lot of gadgets ♪

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:39.734
♪ Sounds like
he's just Elon Musk ♪

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.634
-Wow!
That's fantastic!

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:48.567
[ Laughs ]
Batman is Elon Musk!

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:51.267
[ Laughs ]

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:52.534
Not bad.
That was awesome!

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:55.033
Oh, my gosh.
Fantastic.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:57.133
Give it up once again.
Asa Daniels, right there.

00:05:57.133 --> 00:06:01.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
Asa Daniels.

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:03.868
And now it is time
to see who won,

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:07.133
so we're gonna let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.968
Was it Victoria Skie?

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:13.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:16.300
Or was it Asa Daniels?

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:22.300
Victoria Skie is the winner,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.801
[ Ding! ]

00:06:23.801 --> 00:06:26.234
♪♪

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:32.133
Victoria, you are going home
with $1,000 in an envelope

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.667
and a notebook --

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:36.901
a "Tonight Show" notebook
so you can write more songs.

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.167
-Thank you so much.
-You were very talented.

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.133
Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.400
-Hey.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.934
-Now, no one goes home
empty-handed.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:47.234
You will also be going home
with $1,000

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:48.601
and a "Tonight Show" notebook.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.601 --> 00:06:50.701
-Thank you very much.
-Both of you guys.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.334
Give it up for your two new

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:54.334
instant songwriters,
right there!

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:56.133
Very talented.
Funny. It was awesome.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.467
Thank you so much.

